<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Merrill downgrades EDS.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Merrill downgrades EDS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merrill Lynch said analyst Stephen McClellan downgraded Electronic Data Systems Corp to intermediate-term neutral from accumulate, keeping a long-term accumulate rating on the stock.</p>
<p>-- cited second quarter earnings per share shortfall, and &quot;another sharp reduction in management's forecasts.&quot;</p>
<p>-- cut 1997 earnings per share estimate to $1.90 from $2.30 and 1998 view to $2.20 from $2.65.</p>
<p>-- added &quot;we have only modest confidence in these estimates, pending a return to more normalcy.&quot;</p>
<p>-- stock was off 6-1/16 to 37-1/8.</p>
</text>
